1
00:00:02,400 --> 00:00:04,833
One morning, the king made an announcement.

2
00:00:05,993 --> 00:00:08,711
Starting today, everything you buy is free.

3
00:00:09,671 --> 00:00:10,556
No money.

4
00:00:10,516 --> 00:00:11,580
No bills.

5
00:00:11,830 --> 00:00:12,608
Nothing.

6
00:00:17,900 --> 00:00:19,499
Bob didn't waste a second.

7
00:00:20,459 --> 00:00:21,606
He took a TV.

8
00:00:22,066 --> 00:00:23,058
Then a car.

9
00:00:23,518 --> 00:00:24,629
Then a horse.

10
00:00:25,089 --> 00:00:26,117
Then a piano.

11
00:00:28,767 --> 00:00:30,235
Bob can't play the piano.

12
00:00:30,795 --> 00:00:33,228
But it was free, so now he owns one.

13
00:00:40,333 --> 00:00:41,289
The problem?

14
00:00:41,849 --> 00:00:43,698
Everyone else had the same idea.

15
00:00:45,858 --> 00:00:48,933
By lunchtime, every shelf in the country was empty.

16
00:00:50,583 --> 00:00:52,063
Even the shelves were gone.

17
00:00:52,313 --> 00:00:53,781
Someone took the shelves.

18
00:00:59,767 --> 00:01:01,104
Then things got weird.

19
00:01:02,064 --> 00:01:04,461
If everything is free, why go to work?

20
00:01:06,021 --> 00:01:07,584
The baker stopped baking.

21
00:01:08,944 --> 00:01:10,472
The farmer stopped farming.

22
00:01:11,832 --> 00:01:14,836
And Mr. Gus, the shopkeeper, went fishing.

23
00:01:15,086 --> 00:01:16,030
Permanently.

24
00:01:23,033 --> 00:01:25,085
One week later, Bob was hungry.

25
00:01:26,245 --> 00:01:27,463
He went to the store.

26
00:01:29,023 --> 00:01:30,325
The store was empty.

27
00:01:31,085 --> 00:01:34,518
No food was being made, because nobody was making it.

28
00:01:34,768 --> 00:01:37,462
Free stuff is great, until there is no stuff.

29
00:01:44,767 --> 00:01:47,568
Here's the secret: money isn't just paper.

30
00:01:48,928 --> 00:01:51,599
Prices tell us what's rare and what's valuable.

31
00:01:53,159 --> 00:01:55,663
They also give people a reason to make things.

32
00:01:57,023 --> 00:02:00,027
Take prices away, and the whole system stops.

33
00:02:05,433 --> 00:02:07,378
So the king brought prices back.

34
00:02:07,478 --> 00:02:09,823
King: Okay… prices are back.

35
00:02:10,523 --> 00:02:12,479
Mr. Gus reopened his shop.

36
00:02:13,239 --> 00:02:14,124
And Bob?

37
00:02:14,084 --> 00:02:15,981
Bob tried to return the piano.

38
00:02:16,481 --> 00:02:18,117
Bob: Can I return this?

39
00:02:18,367 --> 00:02:21,883
Turns out, you can't get a refund on something you never paid for.
